<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.987 percent from 9.990 percent posted at the previous auction on February 24.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Sept 2, 1997 (Aug 26, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.987 percent (9.990)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 630.575 million (980.075 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 982.675 million (1,085.275 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.516-10.028 percent (9.800-10.081)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.516-10.200 percent (9.800-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 130 (185)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 174 (188)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
